			"size": {
				"x": 900,
				"y": 200
			},
			"parameters": {},
			"title": "Worn diamond plate",
			"text": "Shared worn diamond plate (structures/common): the civilian, light, heavy, hardened and Castle Brian walls' decks, which tint it with their vertex colours. The tread runs on across repeats, without panel edges or bolts, so the plate tiles without a visible square; the wear is in the roughness, normal and depth, the colour is flat. Based on worn_diamond_plate; metallic 0.8 for the decks' painted steel. Export: File > Export material > Godot > Godot 4 Standard into data/models/board/textures/structures/common (or tools/materials/export.py), then Reload assets in the game's Tuning panel.",
			"color": {
				"type": "Color",
				"r": 0.2,
				"g": 0.25,
				"b": 0.3,
				"a": 1
			}
